Package: rainbowpca
Title: Mapping Continuous Genetic Structure Using RGB-Encoded Principal Components
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Anusha", "Bishop", , "anusha.bishop@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: rainbowpca provides tools for converting principal component (PC) axes into RGB color channels for visualization of multivariate structure across geographic space. The package rescales selected PC axes into red, green, and blue channels, generating composite colors that can be mapped directly onto spatial coordinates. Although designed for visualizing population genetic data, the approach can be applied to any dataset where continuous variation across the first three principal components is of interest.
